Android's BuildLevel (0007e88c) ends each piece of the course at the length of the
segment it picked, also past completion_row_start, where it lays the Finish
segment's rows in place of the pick. A Random: course (Challenge) therefore lays
its finish in pieces as long as the picks and their Padding, each from the
Finish segment's first row, and each piece draws its pick (Segdif) and its
SwitchMirror. Windows ends the piece at the Finish segment's own length and lays
it whole. Courses that list their segments pick the Finish segment itself, so
both lay it whole.

--- a/decomp/game/SubGame/populate_runtime_track_cells_from_segments.cpp
